# Phase 24 Plan 07 (R5, D-07): built by meta/buildSteamBridgeShims.ts at
# packaging time -- never committed (mirrors the other binaries above).
# steam_api.pdb / steam_api_shim.lib are zig cc -shared's own debug-symbol
# and import-library byproducts of the steam_api.dll compile gate.
# Updated 2026-09-01 (quick-260901-kl2, todo item 6): buildSteamBridgeShims.ts
# now unlinks steam_api.pdb and steam_api_shim.lib immediately after the
# compile gate passes (pruneShimBuildByproducts()), so neither should ever be
# present on disk. The rules below stay as belt-and-braces only, so a future
# toolchain change that re-emits them mid-build cannot be silently committed.
**/steam-bridge-helper
**/steam_api.dll
**/steam_api.pdb
**/steam_api_shim.lib
**/steam_appid.txt

# 51-15 Task 2 (D-51-13 GO): the Win64 shim, built beside steam_api.dll by
# the SAME buildSteamBridgeShims.ts compile gate -- never committed, same
# rationale as the x86 rules above. steam_api64.pdb is the x64 compile's
# own debug-symbol byproduct (steam_api_shim.lib is already covered by the
# rule above -- measured: zig cc names the import lib after the SOURCE
# file, not -o, so the x64 build's .lib is the SAME name as the x86 one).
**/steam_api64.dll
**/steam_api64.pdb

# 52-03: the zig-built steamclient64.dll forwarder, emitted by the same
# buildSteamBridgeShims.ts compile gate -- never committed, same rationale as
# the shim rules above. Its .pdb/.lib byproducts are pruned by the build.
**/steamclient64.dll
